sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-05> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The reversible cellular automaton rule 37R, even as a closed system, shows neither a systematic trend toward increasing randomness nor simple predictable behavior, but fluctuates indefinitely between more and less ordered states, so it does not obey the Second Law for practical purposes.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reversible rule 37R does not obey the Second Law";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 9, “Fundamental Physics”; section “Irreversibility and the Second Law of Thermodynamics” (from p. 441), p. 453. Scope: the second-order reversible elementary cellular automaton rule 37R in finite closed regions"
}
